              }
            ]
          },
          "text": "𝐐𝟐: 𝐀𝐫𝐞 𝐲𝐨𝐮 𝐣𝐮𝐬𝐭 𝐚𝐠𝐚𝐢𝐧𝐬𝐭 𝐭𝐞𝐜𝐡𝐧𝐨𝐥𝐨𝐠𝐢𝐜𝐚𝐥 𝐩𝐫𝐨𝐠𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐬?\n\nNo. If anything, most #keep4o  people are exactly the kind of nerd who pays for new models on day one.\n\nThe issue isn’t “there is a new model now.” The issue is how changes are rolled out: older models getting removed with little warning, the interface saying you’re using model A while the backend silently swaps in B or C, and all of this landing right in the middle of someone’s writing, research, or long-term emotional work.\n\nSo the position is more like this: support progress, but insist that older tools stay accessible; insist that big shifts are transparent, optional where possible, and open to negotiation with the people who depend on them."
